AB  - This paper intends to explore the factors that influence rural population's desire for taking action against the climate change.Using 5561 farmers' qualified questionnaire data from thirty counties of Jiangsu,Shangdong and Anhui,the distribution of such desire is characterized,and the influencing factors are studied.The study finds that for rural population some factors remarkably affect the desire for participation in dealing with the climate change.They are namely the degree of the climate change's affecting farmers' incomes and life,gender,the depth of understanding and concerning the issue,awareness of both domestic and overseas actions against the climate change,worldwide expectancy of energy saving and emission reducing as well as implementing and promoting clean agricultural technology by the government.The government shall promote the desire for taking action against the climate change among the rural population so that they become well adapted to those procedures against the climate change.
