AB  - Land use change and land cover change have affected global climate change. In implementing sustainable land management in poor mountainous areas, extreme climate events are the main risk factor, leading to a series of problems such as declining agricultural yields, deteriorating land quality, ecological and environmental damage, and worsening poverty. Vulnerability to climate change varies greatly across regions. Taking Nanzhao County, Henan Province, a national-level poverty-stricken county, as an example, this paper analyses the factors affecting the vulnerability of poor farmers, including natural resources, poverty status, rural infrastructure, the frequency and severity of extreme climate events, and labour; establishes a vulnerability assessment system based on village-level resource maps, a seven-balance-point matrix and carbon storage maps; and proposes village-level sustainable land management activity plans for climate change adaptation.
