AB  - Climate changes are a popular research topic today as well as a focus in eco-anthropology and ethno-ecology.From the gender perspective,this research analyzes the ways and features of the Tibetan women's handling climate changes and disasters in Hongpo Village in Deqin of Yunnan Province.Whether facing immediate or long-term climate changes or disasters,these women could effectively handle them.It is concluded that the measures based on themselves and traditional knowledge as well as external aids is an effective way for establishing a disaster-prevention mechanism.
