AB  - Climate change may affect human production and livelihoods to varying degrees from area to area,and from group to group,and its impacts on the poor in ecologically vulnerable areas are especially special. Choosing-farmers' and herdsmen's livelihoods in ecologically vulnerable areas of Ningxia- typical areas affected by droughts- as an example,this paper attempts to analyze specific impacts of climate change on local farmers' and herdsmen's production,living and subsistence conditions,and degrees of such impacts,and explore key livelihood adaptation measures for farmers and herdsmen to respond to climate change through a questionnaire survey on and interviews with 294 farming and stockbreeding households in five counties/cities/districts of the Ningxia Hui Autonomous Region. The results indicate that the mental self-adjustment of farmers and herdsmen is a prerequisite to response to climate change for vulnerable persons,and they also respond to impacts of climate change by way of livelihood diversification,outside employment, proactive migration and other self-adaptation measures. This also relies on the macroscopic environment of institutional design and policy support by the government.
