TI  - Synergy between Planned and Autonomous Adaptation: The Case of Labour Migrants in Ningxia
TT  - 规划性与自发性适应的协同——以宁夏劳务移民为例
AU  - 孟慧新
KW  - climate change adaptation
KW  - ecological migration
KW  - labour migration
KW  - state-society coordinated development
KW  - Ningxia
AB  - Climate change adaptation is closely linked to poverty eradication and sustainable development. In practice, the degree of synergy between the state's planned adaptation strategies and the autonomous adaptation actions of grassroots society determines the effectiveness of adaptation. In Ningxia, both the government and migrants respond to climate risks through non-farm livelihood transition. The government invests substantial resources for this purpose, while allocating resources by strictly regulating migrants' eligibility and migration behaviour. However, these regulations conflict with the autonomous adaptation actions of migrants in differing circumstances. Each of the two modes of adaptation encounters difficulties, and neither has achieved genuine transition to non-farm livelihoods. Resolving these difficulties requires planned strategies to take seriously the drivers and processes of autonomous adaptation in grassroots society and to explore more practical and effective modes of governance.
