AB  - Although climate change and natural disasters are highly interrelated, the "fragmentation" of international law has caused these two fields to be governed separately. International humanitarian law, human rights law and other bodies of law can integrate climate change and natural disaster issues to a certain extent, but incorporating disaster risk reduction into the international law of climate change adaptation is the key to "issue linkage". The international community should formulate a "Protocol on Climate Change Adaptation", establish the principles and concepts of sustainable development and international solidarity, and set up linkage mechanisms in international finance, early warning, technology and organization, thereby promoting the collaborative governance of climate change and natural disasters under international law.
