AB  - Vulnerability,as a concept,has become a research focus because it provides holistic description of the most prominent effects brought by climate change. Current studies on vulnerability in China concentrate more on natural ecosystems than socio-economic systems,and even less on vulnerability of a regional or specific group to climate change,which is the fundamental basis to understand the status quo and improve the adaptability to climate change. In China,most povertystricken areas are ecologically fragile areas,and they endure more impacts from climate change. Therefore,how to reduce climate poverty is a challenge for China. Social vulnerability,sensibility and adaptability have become important concepts in international climate change research. In order to promote the development of domestic research,this paper reviews existing foreign literatures,and explains the importance of the concept of social vulnerability for poverty reduction in the case of climate change.
