AB  - "Mitigation" and "adaptation" are the two basic strategies for responding to climate change, but related practice and theoretical research have focused mostly on "mitigation", and the construction of climate change adaptation institutions has not received the attention it deserves. The pervasiveness and complexity of climate change cause a time lag in the effects of responses to climate change; therefore, climate change adaptation is an important measure for alleviating current adverse climate impacts. Climate change adaptation involves multiple industries and sectors, and the construction of an adaptation institutional system should be macro-level and systematic; its content should include a climate change adaptation planning system, a climate change impact assessment system, a climate change monitoring, forecasting and early warning system, and a climate change adaptation safeguard system.
