AB  - The utilization and governance of transboundary water involves the issue of resource allocation and environmental management among river basin countries, that is an important issue widely concerned by the international community. The vulnerability of water resources to climate change further exacerbates the complexity of transboundary water governance. China is the most important upstream country in the world, where the major transboundary river basins in Asian continent originate. How to develop transboundary water, tackle climate change and ensure water resources security is a key strategic issue facing China's sustainable development. This research analyzes the management policies and practices from transboundary water basins' action to climate change, and puts forward some suggestions on how to deal with climate change and improve transboundary water resources governance from: river basin governance concept, institution and mechanism construction, strengthening legislation and key research questions.
