TI  - Farmers' Climate Change Adaptation Behaviour and Its Influencing Factors in Major Grain-Producing Areas
TT  - 粮食主产区农民适应气候变化的行为及影响因素研究
AU  - 彭俊杰
KW  - climate change
KW  - major grain-producing areas
KW  - adaptation behaviour
AB  - Research on farmers' adaptation to climate change is an important topic in the current field of climate change research. Based on the analysis and assessment of 1,560 questionnaires, this paper studies the behavioural choices of farmers in major grain-producing areas in adapting to climate change and their influencing factors. The results show that most farmers recognize climate change and its impacts on agricultural production and have adopted various adaptive behaviours, including engineering and non-engineering measures. Gender, educational level, household social capital, water availability, crop type, topographic factors, the timing of access to climate change information sources, and whether the government provides technical, economic and other support policies are the main factors affecting farmers' choices of climate change adaptation behaviour in major grain-producing areas. Therefore, it is recommended that the government strengthen guidance and support in extreme climate event early warning and forecasting services, fiscal policy, basic agricultural capacity building and farmer skills training, so as to continuously enhance the climate change adaptation capacity of farmers in major grain-producing areas.
