AB  - Under the influence of global climate change,the melting rate of glaciers has accelerated,and lakes with glacier melt water as their main source of supply have seen lake level rise. Through the case study of lake Selin co in the Qinghai-Tibet plateau,it is found that the rise of the lake level has flooded a large number of pastures in the surrounding areas,and the decline of animal husbandry has had a serious impact on the livelihood of local herdsmen and the degree of poverty has been deepening. However,the current system of grassland contracting responsi bility weakens the herdsmen' s coping ability,and herdsmen spontaneously organize and cooperate to restore the traditional way of collective use of grassland,using the original local knowledge to adapt to climate change,improving livelihood and cope with environmental problems.
