KW  - climate change
KW  - farmers
KW  - adaptation behaviour
AB  - Through household interviews with farmers in the central Hexi Corridor, this article conducts an in-depth survey covering farmer characteristics, agricultural characteristics, perceptions of climate and adaptation, and finds that most farmers are able to adopt adaptive behaviours in response to climate change, but the types and measures of the adaptive behaviours they adopt differ, as do their effects on agricultural production. Drawing on the survey data, the article examines in depth farmers' adaptive behaviours to climate change and their influencing factors, so as to provide a theoretical reference for farmers' climate change adaptation in other arid and semi-arid regions. The results show that farmers' awareness of climate change, gender and years of farming have a significant positive effect on whether they adopt adaptive behaviours, while farmers' perception of climate change, educational level and years of farming have a significant negative effect on whether they adopt proactive adaptive behaviours. Accordingly, relevant policy recommendations are proposed for farmers' responses to climate change.
