AB  - Adaptation is an important measure for the international community, especially developing countries,to deal with climate change. The nature of public goods for adaptation to climate change determines the complexity of global climate adaptation fund-raising and expenditure. On the basis of systematically combing the principles of raising and spending climate adaptation funds at home and abroad, this paper analyzes the sources of global climate adaptation funds, and uses the CRS system data of the Development Assistance Committee of the organization for economic development and cooperation to describe the temporal and spatial evolution and sectoral distribution of global climate adaptation funds. At present, global adaptation fund-raising and expenditure are characterized by systematicness,synergy, innovation and vulnerability. Its smooth operation requires mutual cooperation and joint efforts of all countries. Under the guidance of the concept of “two communities”, China should adhere to the position of developing countries, continue to explore financial solutions for climate adaptation, and promote the new process of global climate governance.
