AB  - The impact of climate change on economy and society is becoming an important field of empirical research.But so far,domestic research on the effects of climate change is still focused on analyzing the impact of climate change on agriculture.Research on the relationship between climate change and other economic sectors,and the social effects of climate change are still rare.First of all,this paper provides a relatively comprehensive review of a large number of empirical studies on climate change economics that has emerged in international journal in recent years,including both the economic effects of climate change and the social effects of climate change.With the expansion of object and content,new approaches such as long difference approach,long average approach were being developed,dynamic panel model,distributed lags model,polynomial and bin regression equation were being applied.Further research should pay more attention to interdisciplinarity,extend the content and object,explore micro mechanisms of climate change impact and accurately evaluate the effect of adaptation measures.
