AB  - Urban adaptation to climate change is a hot issue in the field of Global Climate Governance and sustainable development. Japan has established a sound legal and policy system of urban adaptation to climate change to promote urban adaptation action, which has a high reference value. This paper reviews the core issues and prominent features of urban adaptation to climate change in Japan at different stages, analyzes the overall framework, main adaptation content, guarantee and support mechanism of urban adaptation, and discusses the specific practice of urban adaptation to climate change in Japan. Combined with the experience of Japan and the actual situation of China, this paper proposes that China should consolidate the scientific basis of urban adaptation to climate change, incorporate the concept of adaptation into urban development planning, improve cross city and cross department cooperation and coordination mechanism, establish multi subject adaptation mechanism, and promote multi-objective coordination, so as to provide some reference and inspiration for China′s urban adaptation to climate change.
