TI  - Measurement of China's adaptive development index (2010-2019)
TT  - 中国适应性发展指数测度(2010-2019年)
AU  - 王宏新
AU  - 邵俊霖
AU  - 李继霞
AU  - 徐孟志
AU  - 王英杰
AU  - 平泽宇
KW  - adaptive development index (ADI)
KW  - climate change
KW  - exposure
KW  - sensitivity
KW  - adaptive capacity
AB  - Adaptive development aims to achieve the goals of growth, equality, and sustainability while stressing adaptation to climate change. On the basis of reviewing the adaptive development theory, this study attempted to define the implications of adaptive development first and then identify the complex interaction between adaptation and development. The research then constructed a comprehensive evaluation index system for adaptive development covering the three dimensions of exposure, sensitivity, and adaptive capacity. To achieve the Adaptive Development Index(ADI) and analyze its spatial and temporal distribution and regional differences, this study applied various quantitative methods, including the CRITIC integration method, the Moran index, coefficient of variation, and the Theil index, by using statistical data from 31 provinces in China from 2010 to 2019. The findings showed that:(1) The overall ADI in China was low and showed a fluctuating upward trend.(2) There were significant differences in the development trends of the three major dimensions, with exposure increasing by 3.39%, sensitivity increasing by 1.07%, and adaptive capacity increasing by 0.7% in 2019 compared to 2010, with adaptive capacity increasing more slowly.(3) Adaptive capacity was the main factor causing the differences in ADI levels.(4) The spatial distribution of ADI had a regional characteristic of ‘East > Center > Northeast > West,' and the influence of intra-regional differences on overall differences gradually exceeded that of inter-regional differences. Furthermore, there was a significant global regional positive correlation among provinces. According to the above findings, we propose initiatives to improve the level of adaptive development in China in terms of top-level design, key areas, and collaborative governance. First, China should adopt a top-level design of adaptive development based on the concept of complex systems, especially the system engineering theory of ecological civilization construction. Second, we should leverage our strengths to make up for our weaknesses and focus on key areas of adaptation actions. Third,we should actively facilitate the integration of adaptive development into major regional development strategies and coordinated development strategies.
