AB  - Climate change has profoundly affected natural-social-economic systems and poses severe challenges to urban construction and development. Through climate change adaptation actions, cities and urban agglomerations can strengthen risk identification and management, enhance system resilience, and effectively mitigate the multidimensional adverse impacts caused by climate. This paper explains the necessity and particularity of climate change adaptation with cities and urban agglomerations as the main actors; on this basis, it analyses the dynamic regulation mechanism of climate adaptation in cities and urban agglomerations, examines adaptation strategies across five dimensions (natural ecology, economy, society, infrastructure and integrated governance), and proposes adaptation schemes for typical urban agglomerations based on regionally heterogeneous climate risk characteristics, providing support for climate resilience building and sustainable development of China's cities and urban agglomerations.
