AB  - The CPC Central Committee's recommendations for the 15th Five-Year Plan emphasize: "Improve the climate change adaptation work system and enhance capacity to respond to climate change, especially extreme weather." At present, global warming combined with events such as El Niño has caused many parts of China to experience record-breaking, disaster-inducing extreme weather events; in 2024, direct economic losses from natural disasters nationwide exceeded 400 billion yuan. Although China has launched climate-resilient city pilot construction, most cities have not yet adopted the concept of active and proactive climate change adaptation; urban functional and ecological buffer redundancy is insufficient, the climate vulnerability of "infrastructure" is relatively high, and emergency monitoring capacity and early warning and response mechanisms urgently need strengthening. There is a pressing need to fully integrate climate change adaptation into the overall economic and social development agenda, advance the modernization of the climate change adaptation governance system and governance capacity, and provide resilience safeguards for promoting urban modernization with Chinese characteristics.
