AB  - This paper constructs an analytical framework of "content-tool-evaluation", adopts policy content analysis and policy consistency index modeling methods, conducts text analysis and quantitative evaluation of the regional "Action Plans for Climate Change Adaptation" in China. The research findings are as follows:(1) The policy content exhibits hierarchical governance characteristics of "target-oriented-action coordination-policy support", and enhances regional climate adaptability through the decomposition of quantitative indicators, coordinated actions in multiple fields, and the strengthening of institutional safeguards.(2) In terms of policy tool configuration, each region presents a differentiated pattern of "administrative dominance > social empowerment > market lag".(3) The climate adaptation policies in China are generally at a good level. The core economic regions in East China and North China lead by virtue of the advantages of resource aggregation and institutional innovation. The Southwest, Northwest, and Central China comprehensively utilize ecological restoration tools to exert policy effectiveness, while South China and Northeast China lag relatively due to the homogeneous natural base and insufficient tool innovation. Based on this, this paper puts forward optimization suggestions from three aspects: optimizing the policy tool portfolio, deepening regional joint prevention and control, and strengthening scientific and technological empowerment.
