AB  - Taking appropriate climate change adaptation measures(CCAM) is a better way for farmers to resist climate change risks. However, farmers' CCAM are not only dependent on objective livelihood resilience(OLR) but also affected by their subjective livelihood resilience(SLR). Farmers' OLR and SLR deviation may further affect their CCAM. By using the survey data from 540 farmers in Sichuan Province,a research path of“livelihood resilience→livelihood strategy”is constructed based on the sustainable livelihood framework,and the correlation between farmers' OLR and SLR deviation and CCAM is explored. Results show that the OLR and SLR deviation is common among the surveyed farmers,and 57. 78% of the farmers have higher SLR than OLR. Farmers' OLR and SLR deviation has a positive and significant impact on the active CCAM,but has no significant effect on passive CCAM. In addition,gender,age,health status,marital status and disaster experience of farmers have significant impact on their active CCAM either.
