AB  - Since the new era, China has actively participated in international climate legislation such as the Paris Agreement and, in response to the domestic codification of the Ecological Environment Code, major breakthroughs have been made in climate change adaptation legislation. The Ecological Environment Code establishes the basic logic of climate change adaptation legislation, including clarifying the core demands for inclusion in the Code, the transformation and application of environmental policies and laws, and the legislative rules for separate laws under a dual-source-of-law structure, laying the codified foundation for climate change adaptation legislation. The Ecological Environment Code establishes "basic law" norms for climate change adaptation, including basic principles, norms on actors, and adaptation measures, while reserving external legislative space for local regulations or rules, thereby forming a legal system for climate change adaptation legislation. In the era of codification, climate change adaptation legislation achieves inter-legal coordination by handling its relationship with "mitigation", legislative coordination, and international cooperation. Thus, the specialized status of climate change adaptation legislation within the ecological environment legal system is clarified, ensuring that climate adaptation governance is rule-of-law-based, institutionalized and science-based.
