TI  - On the Institutional System and Legislative Expression of Climate Law
TT  - 气候法的制度体系及其立法表达
AU  - 徐以祥
AU  - 高愚
KW  - climate law
KW  - institutional system
KW  - Ecological Environment Code
KW  - single-subject legislation
AB  - China's Eco-Environmental Code establishes an independent volume for green and lowcarbon development. Chapter IV thereof, addressing climate change, lays a principled and framework foundation for constructing the institutional system of climate law, clarifying the core institutional directions including climate change mitigation, adaptation, and international cooperation.Nevertheless, since the provisions of the Code focus on guidance and fundamental principles, supporting special laws are still required to improve the climate law system. In the post-Code era, how to construct a scientific institutional system of climate law and realize its legislative expression has become a key urgent issue for the development of China's rule of law on climate governance. The construction of the climate law institutional system is inevitable, stemming from the complexity of climate issues, the diversity of climate law objectives, and the pluralism of governance approaches. This institutional system consists of four sub-systems: climate change mitigation, climate adaptation, support and guarantee, and international coordination.Institutional development shall balance the two core pillars of mitigation and adaptation. Legislatively, a “1+2+N” framework should be established: the Eco-Environmental Code serves as the general outline to provide principled guidance; the Climate Change Mitigation Act and Climate Change Adaptation Act function as the core laws to specify concrete mechanisms; and various supporting normative documents supplement detailed provisions. This will form a hierarchically clear, coordinated and efficient climate law system, delivering solid legal safeguards for China's response to climate change.
