TI  - Can Climate Change Adaptation Policy Promote Corporate Innovation?——A Quasi-Natural Experiment Based on Climate-Resilient City Development
TT  - 适应气候变化政策能促进企业创新吗——基于气候适应型城市建设的准自然实验
AU  - 邹梦琪
AU  - 程婧妍
AU  - 王帆
KW  - climate-adaptive cities
KW  - environmental uncertainty
KW  - government support
KW  - corporate resilience
KW  - corporate innovation
AB  - In the context of climate change, exploring the impact of climate adaptation policies on corporate innovation is of great significance. Using the pilot program of climate-resilient city construction as a quasi-natural experiment, this study investigates the influence of climate adaptation policies with Chinese characteristics on corporate innovation. The results show that the pilot policy significantly promotes corporate innovation, primarily by reducing environmental uncertainty faced by firms, increasing government support, and enhancing corporate resilience. This facilitating effect is more pronounced in the following types of samples: state-owned enterprises, heavily polluting firms, and those with strong dynamic capabilities; regions facing higher climate risk and lacking sufficient pre-existing adaptation capacity; and local governments with abundant financial resources, strong governance capacity, and a lower degree of fiscal decentralization. Further analysis reveals that the pilot policy can enhance the quality and efficiency of corporate innovation, thereby improving corporate productivity and expected value, while also generating positive regional spillover effects. This study identifies key institutional factors influencing corporate innovation in the context of climate change, providing empirical evidence for improving relevant institutional arrangements, better adapting to climate change, and promoting high-quality development.
