TI  - How Will China Build a Climate-Adaptive Society?
TT  - 我国将如何建成气候适应型社会?
AU  - 徐若冰
KW  - climate change
KW  - climate-adaptive society
KW  - natural ecosystems
KW  - socio-economic systems
AB  - Building a climate-adaptive society essentially means raising the level of climate adaptation by enhancing the risk identification and response capacities of natural ecosystems and socio-economic systems. In recent years, China has made great achievements in building a climate-adaptive society: the relevant policy system has been steadily improved, climate monitoring and early warning have steadily advanced, climate change adaptation capacity in key sectors and regions has gradually increased, climate-resilient city construction has progressed steadily, public awareness of climate adaptation has continued to grow, and international cooperation on climate adaptation has continued to deepen. However, given the requirements of high-quality development, the new security architecture and the modernization of national governance capacity, and in the face of various shortcomings in the adaptation process, further advancing the building of a climate-adaptive society remains highly necessary and urgent. To this end, in further advancing the building of a climate-adaptive society, China should continue to improve the climate change adaptation policy system, refine the climate change adaptation organizational system, strengthen climate change risk identification capacity, carry out climate change adaptation actions in key sectors and regions, and increase the input of factor resources into climate change adaptation.
